```json
{
  "issues": [
    {
      "criterion_id": "api_surface.changes[0]",
      "type": "ambiguous",
      "description": "The api_surface changes block states 'do not introduce new error variants or map_err wrapping', yet AC-3 requires returning Err(GraphError::UnexpectedManifestVersion { ... }), which is a new error variant not present in the existing GraphError enum. A developer reading this literally cannot satisfy both constraints simultaneously. The spec must either (a) confirm this variant already exists in GraphError and cite its current definition, or (b) remove the 'no new error variants' constraint and replace it with the explicit struct definition of UnexpectedManifestVersion including field names and types.",
      "suggested_fix": "Replace 'do not introduce new error variants or map_err wrapping' with: 'Add one new GraphError variant: UnexpectedManifestVersion { path: PathBuf, expected_from: Version, expected_to: Version, found: Version }. All other error propagation uses the existing ? operator with no new From impls or map_err calls.'"
    },
    {
      "criterion_id": "AC-3",
      "type": "ambiguous",
      "description": "'No path is pushed to modified_paths for this bump' is ambiguous when a bump has multiple writes entries and earlier entries have already been successfully processed before the failing entry is reached. It is unclear whether (a) only the erroring target's path is withheld, leaving previously pushed paths in modified_paths, or (b) no path from any target in the failing bump appears in modified_paths at all (implying a rollback of already-pushed entries). AC-7 has the same ambiguity for write_version errors.",
      "suggested_fix": "Append to AC-3: 'Paths already pushed to modified_paths by earlier writes entries within the same bump prior to encountering the unexpected version are NOT removed — modified_paths retains whatever was accumulated before the failing entry. The phrase no path is pushed for this bump refers only to the failing target and all remaining unprocessed targets in this bump.' Apply the same clarification to AC-7."
    },
    {
      "criterion_id": "AC-6",
      "type": "missing-error-case",
      "description": "AC-6 specifies the absent-file case (file does not exist → Ok, path staged) and the present-file case (file exists → removed), but does not specify what happens when fs::remove_file fails for a reason other than file-not-found (e.g., EACCES, EROFS, EISDIR). A developer must decide whether to propagate the IO error or ignore it — the spec gives no guidance.",
      "suggested_fix": "Add: 'When fs::remove_file returns an error for a reason other than the file being absent (e.g., permission denied), apply_version_plan propagates that Err immediately via the ? operator, wrapping it as Err(GraphError::Io(_)) or the existing IO error variant on GraphError. The changeset path is NOT pushed to modified_paths in this case.'"
    },
    {
      "criterion_id": "AC-4",
      "type": "untestable",
      "description": "'ManifestFormat::from_path only inspects the file extension and does not fail' is an implementation assumption about a dependency's behavior, not a testable proposition for apply_version_plan. It cannot be verified by a test of apply_version_plan itself, and it silently constrains the test design without being framed as a non-goal or scope note.",
      "suggested_fix": "Move this sentence out of AC-4 and into the spec's scope field as: 'ManifestFormat::from_path is assumed infallible for paths with a recognized extension; test fixtures may use any extension handled by that function without triggering a ManifestError. Extension-validation behavior is out of scope for this spec.' Remove it from AC-4 entirely."
    },
    {
      "criterion_id": null,
      "type": "missing-error-case",
      "description": "The spec does not specify behavior when plan.bumps is an empty slice or when a single bump's writes array is empty. A developer implementing the write loop must decide whether to return Ok with an empty staged list or treat empty input as an error. The consumed_changesets loop has the same gap for an empty changeset list.",
      "suggested_fix": "Add a criterion: 'AC-11: When plan.bumps is empty, or when all bumps have empty writes and consumed_changesets arrays, apply_version_plan returns Ok and ApplyOutcome::staged is an empty Vec. Empty input is not an error.'"
    }
  ],
  "overall": "fail",
  "reasoning": "The spec is unusually precise for its scope — criterion IDs, PartialEq semantics, and exact error propagation mechanics are all well-specified. However, four blocking issues prevent a clean handoff: (1) a direct contradiction between the api_surface constraint ('no new error variants') and AC-3's required new variant forces the implementer to guess which instruction to follow; (2) AC-3 and AC-7 are genuinely ambiguous about whether already-pushed paths from earlier targets in the same failing bump are retracted; (3) fs::remove_file failure modes beyond file-not-found are entirely unaddressed in AC-6; and (4) AC-4 embeds an untestable implementation assumption about a dependency rather than stating a testable proposition. The empty-input case is a lesser gap but still requires a judgment call. All five issues have narrow, low-effort fixes — the spec is one revision away from passing."
}
```

