{
  "schema": "spec@1",
  "id": "SPEC-002",
  "purpose": "Make [[package]] rule lookup specificity-ordered so a prefixed pattern (cargo:foo) always wins over a bare pattern (foo) regardless of TOML declaration order, and emit a warning diagnostic when a bare rule matches packages in more than one ecosystem.",
  "scope": "Two changes in ManifestWalkResolver::build in crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs: (1) the [[package]] rule lookup on line ~154, and (2) a new cross-ecosystem diagnostic pass after the packages loop. One new DiagnosticCode variant added to crates/callisto-model/src/diagnostic.rs. PackageId::matches() is NOT changed.",
  "non_goals": [
    "PackageId::matches() in identity.rs: bare-matches-all-ecosystems is correct and intentional. The fix is at the call site, not in the type.",
    "[[package-set]] rules: multi-ecosystem glob matching is their explicit purpose; they are exempt from the cross-ecosystem diagnostic.",
    "Specificity ordering among multiple Prefixed matches with different ecosystems: first-match-wins (declaration order) is correct for that case.",
    "Specificity ordering among multiple Bare matches: first-match-wins (declaration order) is unchanged.",
    "No new E-code is added: the diagnostic is a Warning, not a miette-diagnosed Error.",
    "Deduplication of identical PackageId entries in cfg.packages is out of scope; the diagnostic pass iterates the Vec as-is, so two identical Bare entries each produce their own diagnostic if both qualify."
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    {
      "id": "AC-1",
      "description": "When cfg.packages contains at least one Prefixed PackageId rule (ecosystem() is Some) and at least one Bare PackageId rule (ecosystem() is None) that all match the same package, the first-matching Prefixed rule in declaration order has its PackageConfig applied to that package (first-match-wins within the Prefixed tier), regardless of how many Bare rules are also present and regardless of their declaration order relative to the Prefixed rules.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-2",
      "description": "When the set of [[package]] rules in cfg.packages that match a given package consists entirely of Bare PackageId rules (no Prefixed rule in cfg.packages matches that package — other Prefixed rules matching different packages may still be present in the Vec), the first-matching Bare rule in declaration order is applied to that package.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-3",
      "description": "When the set of [[package]] rules in cfg.packages that match a given package consists entirely of Prefixed PackageId rules (no Bare rule in cfg.packages matches that package — other Bare rules that match different packages may still be present in the Vec), the first-matching Prefixed rule in declaration order is applied to that package.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-4a",
      "description": "When no [[package]] rule in cfg.packages matches a given package but a [[package-set]] rule does match, the [[package-set]] rule's PackageConfig is returned for that package. When multiple [[package-set]] rules match, the first matching rule in cfg.package_sets declaration order is applied (first-match-wins).",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-4b",
      "description": "When no [[package]] rule and no [[package-set]] rule matches a given package, None is returned for that package.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-5",
      "description": "For each Bare PackageId rule in cfg.packages whose PackageId::matches() predicate returns true for packages from two or more distinct ecosystems among the packages present in the packages map produced by the current ManifestWalkResolver::build invocation (regardless of whether a higher-specificity Prefixed rule governs some of those packages), exactly one Diagnostic is pushed for that rule. Only packages whose PackageId key is Prefixed (ecosystem() returns Some) contribute to the distinct-ecosystem count; Bare-keyed packages (ecosystem() returns None) are excluded and do not affect the count. N qualifying Bare rules (including duplicates — cfg.packages is iterated as-is) produce N diagnostics total. Each diagnostic has: severity = Warning, code = DiagnosticCode::BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems (new variant), and a message that contains the pattern's name string (pattern.name()) as a contiguous substring and, for each Ecosystem value E that appears in the distinct-ecosystem set computed above (i.e., E is the ecosystem() value of at least one Prefixed-keyed package in the packages map that the Bare rule matched), that ecosystem's Ecosystem::prefix() value (e.g. \"cargo\", \"npm\") as a contiguous substring. The message format is otherwise unconstrained. Example acceptable message: \"bare rule \\\"foo\\\" matches packages in multiple ecosystems: cargo, npm\".",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-6",
      "description": "When the distinct-ecosystem count computed per AC-5 for a Bare PackageId rule is zero or one — including the case where the rule matches packages whose PackageId key is Bare (ecosystem() returns None) but no packages whose PackageId key is Prefixed — no diagnostic is pushed for that rule.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-7",
      "description": "Prefixed PackageId rules in cfg.packages never trigger the cross-ecosystem diagnostic regardless of what they match.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-8",
      "description": "Rules in cfg.package_sets never trigger the cross-ecosystem diagnostic regardless of what they match.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-9",
      "description": "When cfg.packages is empty, no diagnostic is pushed and the [[package]]-tier lookup returns None for every queried package. The [[package-set]]-tier fallback (AC-4a) continues to apply normally — if cfg.package_sets is non-empty, it may still return a PackageConfig.",
      "is_error_case": false
    }
  ],
  "api_surface": {
    "file": "crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs",
    "changes": [
      "Replace the cfg.packages.iter().find(...) call (the [[package]] lookup, ~line 154) with a two-pass search: first pass finds any Prefixed-pattern match (pattern.ecosystem().is_some()); second pass (only if first is None) finds any Bare-pattern match. Both passes use first-match-wins within their tier. Result is the same Option<&PackageConfig> type as before.",
      "After the packages loop (after packages.insert), add a pass over cfg.packages: for each (pattern, _) where pattern.ecosystem().is_none() (Bare), collect the distinct ecosystems of all packages in the just-built packages map whose id is matched by pattern. If the ecosystem count is > 1, push one Diagnostic { code: DiagnosticCode::BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems, severity: DiagnosticSeverity::Warning, message: format!(...), package: None, path: None, .. }."
    ],
    "new_variants": [
      "DiagnosticCode::BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems in crates/callisto-model/src/diagnostic.rs — add to the end of the DiagnosticCode enum, kebab-case serde name 'bare-rule-matches-multiple-ecosystems'."
    ]
  }
}

