      "suggested_fix": "Add an AC-010b: 'Running `callisto matrix --format json` against a workspace containing a package.json with malformed JSON syntax (e.g. a trailing comma) exits with code 1 and prints an error identifying the unreadable/malformed manifest path; no MatrixReport JSON is printed to stdout.' mirroring AC-010's structure exactly."
    },
    {
      "criterion_id": "AC-001,AC-002",
      "type": "missing-error-case",
      "description": "No criterion specifies behavior when a single package declares both napi.targets (package.json) and [tool.maturin].targets (pyproject.toml) in the same registered package. PlatformTargetGroup.kind is a single enum value per package-keyed map entry (BTreeMap<String, PlatformTargetGroup>), so it's undefined whether this is an error, whether one source silently wins, or whether the map key collides and overwrites silently.",
      "suggested_fix": "Add an explicit criterion, e.g.: 'When a single registered package has both a napi.targets declaration and a [tool.maturin].targets declaration, callisto matrix returns Err(GraphError::...) naming the package and both conflicting sources; this is a hard error, not a silent last-write-wins.' Or, if dual-toolchain packages are legitimate, specify the disambiguation key (e.g. two synthetic map keys `pkgname` and `pkgname:maturin`) explicitly rather than leaving it to the implementer."
    },
    {
      "criterion_id": "AC-011",
      "type": "incomplete",
      "description": "The spec introduces a new DiagnosticCode variant ('DiagnosticCode::UnrecognisedPlatformTriple or equivalent') but the scope has no requirement to add a row to the diagnostic attribution table at docs/01-spec.md §G.13, unlike track-e (SPEC-002), which treats that table update as a hard AC (AC-11) for its new BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems variant. The DiagnosticCode enum (crates/callisto-model/src/diagnostic.rs:91) is documented at docs/01-spec.md:8315 '### G.13 Diagnostic attribution map' as the canonical registry; leaving a variant out of it is an established repo convention violation, not a stylistic choice.",
      "suggested_fix": "Add to scope: 'Add a row to the diagnostic attribution table at docs/01-spec.md §G.13 for the new DiagnosticCode variant, with Emitted-by referencing the matrix module, and appropriate escalated_by/governed_by placeholders,' and pin the exact variant name (see next finding) so the doc row and the code agree."
    },
    {
      "criterion_id": "api_surface:callisto_graph::commands::matrix",
      "type": "ambiguous",
      "description": "'new DiagnosticCode::UnrecognisedPlatformTriple or equivalent' leaves the exact variant name (and therefore its serde kebab-case wire value) to the implementer's discretion, with no AC pinning it. Every existing DiagnosticCode variant has an exact, spec-fixed name (see SPEC-002's AC-10, which fixes the exact string 'bare-rule-matches-multiple-ecosystems'). Without a fixed name here, two implementers following this spec could diverge, and any downstream consumer (CI, docs) has nothing stable to match against.",
      "suggested_fix": "Fix the exact name: 'Add `DiagnosticCode::UnrecognisedPlatformTriple` to crates/callisto-model/src/diagnostic.rs (kebab-case serde value \"unrecognised-platform-triple\")' — remove 'or equivalent' and add an AC asserting the serialized string, mirroring SPEC-002 AC-10."
    },
    {
      "criterion_id": "AC-016",
      "type": "ambiguous",
      "description": "'(or an equivalent shell pipeline producing the same jq expression)' admits two interpretations: an implementer could read this as 'the exact jq filter text must appear verbatim' or 'any pipeline that is behaviorally equivalent for some restructuring of the shell code is acceptable' (e.g. splitting into two steps, using `jq -c`, reformatting the filter with different whitespace/quoting). Since this is the only AC governing action.yml and it's a hard AC (not is_error_case), the acceptance bar needs to be mechanically checkable.",
      "suggested_fix": "State the check precisely: 'action.yml's NATIVE_MATRIX assignment line, after `jq` is applied to the output of `callisto matrix --format json`, is byte-for-byte parseable as the same jq program `[.platformTargets[].targets[]] | unique_by(.artifactName)` (whitespace-insensitive); the shell wrapper (variable names, quoting style) may differ, but the jq filter argument must not.'"
    },
    {
      "criterion_id": "scope",
      "type": "ambiguous",
      "description": "Scope says the reading/assembly logic lives in a new module 'crates/callisto-graph/src/matrix.rs', but api_surface names the public function 'callisto_graph::commands::matrix' — implying crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/matrix.rs, alongside status.rs/publish.rs/etc. It's unstated whether both files should exist (matrix.rs holding read/derive logic, commands/matrix.rs a thin CommandRunner-generic wrapper calling into it — mirroring how commands/publish.rs calls into apply.rs/groups.rs), or whether 'crates/callisto-graph/src/matrix.rs' is just imprecise phrasing for the single commands/matrix.rs file.",
      "suggested_fix": "State explicitly: 'crates/callisto-graph/src/matrix.rs contains the manifest-reading and MatrixReport-assembly logic (private helpers); crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/matrix.rs contains the public `pub fn matrix<R: CommandRunner, D: DependencyResolver>(...)` entry point that calls into matrix.rs, mirroring the commands/publish.rs -> apply.rs/groups.rs pattern.'"
    }
  ],
  "overall": "fail",
  "reasoning": "Codebase premise claims (triple table, absence of maturin/engines.node readers, absence of MatrixReport types, absence of Command::Matrix, action.yml stub) all check out against the real source. No scope overlap with track-b/e/f. But the api_surface for the core graph-layer function has two compile-blocking errors (CliError used across a reverse-dependency boundary; Workspace referenced without its required generics) that a developer would hit immediately and have to guess the fix for — that alone fails the 'implement without asking a question' bar. Additional gaps: asymmetric error-case coverage (TOML malformed but not JSON malformed), unspecified dual-napi/maturin-declaration behavior, an unfixed DiagnosticCode variant name with no doc-table update requirement (breaking an established repo convention from SPEC-002), and two ambiguous 'or equivalent' escape hatches (AC-016's jq pipeline, module placement) that leave implementation-critical decisions unstated."
}
```

file.content:
{
  "schema": "spec@1",
  "id": "SPEC-004",
  "purpose": "Add a `callisto matrix` CLI subcommand that reads napi-rs and maturin native build target declarations plus npm/PyPI runtime-version constraints from workspace manifests, and emits a deterministic, structured MatrixReport (JSON or human-readable table) that CI workflows consume as the source of truth for build matrices, eliminating hand-maintained YAML drift.",
  "scope": "New `callisto matrix [--package <name>] [--format json|table]` CLI subcommand (crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/matrix.rs, wired into crates/callisto-cli/src/cli.rs `Command::Matrix`). A new `crates/callisto-graph/src/matrix.rs` module that: (1) reads napi.targets from package.json via the existing NapiTargetsIndex/group-walking machinery in crates/callisto-graph/src/napi.rs and, for each declared triple, calls the existing `triple_to_role` to validate recognition then derives platform/arch/abi from the returned `ManifestRole::Platform`, WITHOUT modifying napi.rs; (2) reads `[tool.maturin].targets` from pyproject.toml (new read path in crates/callisto-manifests/src/python.rs or a narrowly-scoped read inside matrix.rs if adding it to python.rs is out of proportion -- implementer's call, but the triple recognition MUST reuse `triple_to_role`, not a second table); (3) reads `engines.node` from package.json and `requires-python` from pyproject.toml as raw strings; (4) derives hostRunner/useCross/artifactName for each recognised triple via a NEW per-triple lookup table in matrix.rs (keyed on the exact triple strings `triple_to_role` actually recognises today: `aarch64-apple-darwin`, `x86_64-apple-darwin`, `x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu`, `x86_64-unknown-linux-musl`, `aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu`, `aarch64-unknown-linux-musl`, `x86_64-pc-windows-msvc`, `i686-pc-windows-msvc`, `aarch64-pc-windows-msvc`, `armv7-unknown-linux-gnueabihf`, `x86_64-unknown-freebsd`, `aarch64-linux-android`, `armv7-linux-androideabi`, `riscv64gc-unknown-linux-gnu`, `powerpc64le-unknown-linux-gnu`, `s390x-unknown-linux-gnu`, `wasm32-wasip1`, `wasm32-unknown-unknown` -- this list differs from the design doc's illustrative table in .claude/specs/callisto-matrix.md section 3.1, which is stale prose, not code; the code table in napi.rs is authoritative per REQ-007); (5) assembles, sorts, and serializes the MatrixReport. New public types MatrixReport, PlatformTargetGroup, PlatformTarget (no `rid` field), RuntimeVersionEntry (no `targetFrameworks`/dotnet fields) live in crates/callisto-model/src/matrix.rs (or crates/callisto-graph/src/matrix.rs if the maintainer prefers graph-layer placement -- either is acceptable provided the types derive Serialize/Deserialize and PartialEq for testability; this spec fixes the location as crates/callisto-model/src/matrix.rs for consistency with other report types such as StatusReport). Updates to .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml to replace the existing `{\"platformTargets\":{}}` stub with a call to the real subcommand piped through the jq expression specified in REQ-007's done_when list.",
  "non_goals": [
    "dotnet-aot target kind: no .NET RID table, no reading of <TargetFramework>/<TargetFrameworks>/<RuntimeIdentifiers> from .csproj files, no PlatformTarget.rid field, no MSBuild/XML parsing of any kind. Deferred to a follow-up track; callisto-manifests has zero .NET/XML support today.",
    "Java (Maven/Gradle) and dotnet RuntimeVersionEntry ecosystem values ('java', 'dotnet'). The RuntimeVersionEntry.ecosystem field in this spec is a closed enum of exactly 'npm' and 'python'; adding 'java'/'dotnet' variants is follow-up work, not a forward-compatible placeholder implemented here.",
    "The dotnet-aot dispatch block in a callisto-build-action composite action (design doc section 7.2, kind=dotnet-aot).",
    "Creating the callisto-build-action composite action itself is optional for this spec -- the CLI subcommand and its JSON contract are the hard requirement; the composite action (napi/maturin dispatch blocks) may ship in the same cycle if time allows but its absence does not block spec completion.",
    "YAML generation for GitHub Actions workflows beyond the single jq-piped nativeMatrix output line specified in REQ-007.",
    "Inferring maturin targets from manylinux compat tags; the matrix reader requires explicit `[tool.maturin] targets = [...]` and does no compat-tag inference.",
    "Fetching current LTS/version-support data from external services (Node release schedule, PyPI classifiers) to expand engines.node/requires-python ranges into discrete version lists. Ranges are emitted as raw manifest strings only, with zero HTTP calls (hermetic-by-design invariant).",
    "Any modification to napi.rs's existing triple_to_role/role_to_triple functions, their triple table, or NapiTargetsIndex's existing drift-detection behavior. matrix.rs is a read-only consumer of triple_to_role.",
    "Discrete version-range parsing/validation of engines.node or requires-python (e.g. semver range validation, PEP 440 validation). The range string is passed through verbatim with no syntax checking; a malformed range string is not a matrix-command error.",
    "Support for maturin/napi packages that declare targets via mechanisms other than the exact manifest fields `napi.targets` (package.json) and `[tool.maturin].targets` (pyproject.toml) -- e.g. environment-variable-driven or Cargo.toml-embedded target lists are not read.",
    "Caching or incremental recomputation of the matrix report across invocations; each `callisto matrix` invocation performs a full manifest walk."
  ],
  "api_surface": [
    {
      "name": "MatrixReport",
      "signature": "pub struct MatrixReport { pub platform_targets: BTreeMap<String, PlatformTargetGroup>, pub runtime_versions: BTreeMap<String, RuntimeVersionEntry> } // serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\") -> {\"platformTargets\":{...},\"runtimeVersions\":{...}}",
      "description": "Top-level report type returned by callisto_graph::commands::matrix() and serialized as the --format json output. BTreeMap guarantees lexicographic key ordering by registered package name without a separate sort step. An empty report serializes to {\"platformTargets\":{},\"runtimeVersions\":{}}."
    },
    {
      "name": "PlatformTargetGroup",
      "signature": "pub struct PlatformTargetGroup { pub kind: PlatformTargetKind, pub source: String, pub targets: Vec<PlatformTarget> } ; pub enum PlatformTargetKind { Napi, Maturin } // serde(rename_all = \"lowercase\") -> \"napi\" | \"maturin\"",
      "description": "One package's native-build target group. `source` is the raw manifest field name ('napi.targets' or '[tool.maturin].targets'), used for audit output only -- not a filesystem path. `targets` is sorted by triple string before serialization. PlatformTargetKind deliberately omits a DotnetAot variant; adding one is out of scope for this spec."
    },
    {
      "name": "PlatformTarget",
      "signature": "pub struct PlatformTarget { pub triple: String, pub platform: String, pub arch: String, pub abi: Option<String>, pub host_runner: String, pub use_cross: bool, pub artifact_name: String, pub package_dir: String, pub package_name: String } // serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")",
      "description": "One platform build target within a PlatformTargetGroup. No `rid` field (napi/maturin only, no dotnet-aot). `abi` serializes as JSON null when None (darwin, freebsd, android, wasi/unknown-wasm32 targets and all win32 targets carry no abi). `triple` and derived platform/arch/abi come from callisto_graph::napi::triple_to_role; host_runner/use_cross/artifact_name come from the new per-triple table in matrix.rs. `package_dir` is workspace-root-relative."
    },
    {
      "name": "RuntimeVersionEntry",
      "signature": "pub struct RuntimeVersionEntry { pub ecosystem: RuntimeEcosystem, pub field: String, pub range: String } ; pub enum RuntimeEcosystem { Npm, Python } // serde(rename_all = \"lowercase\") -> \"npm\" | \"python\"",
      "description": "One package's runtime-version constraint, sourced from engines.node (npm) or requires-python (python/PyPI). `range` is the raw, unvalidated manifest string. No targetFrameworks field (dotnet-only, out of scope)."
    },
    {
      "name": "callisto_graph::commands::matrix",
      "signature": "pub fn matrix<R: CommandRunner>(ws: &Workspace, opts: &MatrixOptions) -> Result<MatrixReport, CliError> ; pub struct MatrixOptions { pub package: Option<String> }",
      "description": "Builds the MatrixReport for the workspace (or a single package when opts.package is Some). Returns Err when opts.package names a package not present in the workspace's registered package set, and Err on any manifest read/parse failure (unreadable file, malformed TOML/JSON). Emits a warning-level Diagnostic (new DiagnosticCode::UnrecognisedPlatformTriple or equivalent) per unrecognised napi/maturin triple encountered and excludes that triple from targets[] without failing the call."
    },
    {
      "name": "callisto matrix (CLI subcommand)",
      "signature": "callisto matrix [--package <name>] [--format json|table]",
      "description": "New Command::Matrix(MatrixArgs) variant in crates/callisto-cli/src/cli.rs and handler in crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/matrix.rs. --format defaults to the global --format flag's value where applicable but this subcommand additionally accepts its own --format json|table (json is default). --package restricts output to one registered package name. Exit code 0 on success including an empty report; exit code 1 on a manifest read/parse error. Unknown --package name is also an exit-code-1 error with a message naming the unknown package (not a silent empty report)."
    }
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    {
      "id": "AC-001",
      "criterion": "In a workspace containing a group with a napi package.json declaring napi.targets = [\"aarch64-apple-darwin\", \"x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu\"], running `callisto matrix --format json` produces a platformTargets entry keyed by the group's registered package name, with kind:\"napi\", source:\"napi.targets\", and targets[] containing exactly 2 PlatformTarget objects whose triple/platform/arch/abi fields match the values returned by callisto_graph::napi::triple_to_role for each of those two triples.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-002",
      "criterion": "In a workspace containing a pyproject.toml with [tool.maturin].targets = [\"x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu\", \"aarch64-apple-darwin\"], running `callisto matrix --format json` produces a platformTargets entry with kind:\"maturin\", source:\"[tool.maturin].targets\", and targets[] whose platform/arch/abi/hostRunner/useCross values for each triple are identical to the values produced for the same triple string in a napi group in AC-001 -- i.e. the triple-to-platform-attributes derivation is provably shared code, not a duplicated table.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-003",
      "criterion": "In a workspace with no napi.targets fields, no [tool.maturin].targets fields, no engines.node fields, and no requires-python fields anywhere, running `callisto matrix --format json` prints exactly {\"platformTargets\":{},\"runtimeVersions\":{}} to stdout and the process exits with code 0.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-004",
      "criterion": "In a workspace with an npm package whose package.json contains \"engines\": {\"node\": \">=20.0.0\"}, running `callisto matrix --format json` produces a runtimeVersions entry for that package's registered name equal to {\"ecosystem\":\"npm\",\"field\":\"engines.node\",\"range\":\">=20.0.0\"}.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-005",
      "criterion": "In a workspace with a PyPI package whose pyproject.toml contains requires-python = \">=3.9\", running `callisto matrix --format json` produces a runtimeVersions entry for that package's registered name equal to {\"ecosystem\":\"python\",\"field\":\"requires-python\",\"range\":\">=3.9\"}.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-006",
      "criterion": "In a workspace with two or more napi/maturin/runtime-version-bearing packages, running `callisto matrix --package <one-registered-name> --format json` produces a report containing only that package's entries in platformTargets and runtimeVersions (all other packages' keys absent from both maps).",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-007",
      "criterion": "Running `callisto matrix --package does-not-exist --format json` in any workspace exits with code 1 and prints a human-readable error message that names \"does-not-exist\" as an unrecognised package; it does not print a structurally valid empty MatrixReport.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-008",
      "criterion": "Running `callisto matrix --format table` in a workspace with at least one napi target and one runtime-version entry produces non-JSON, human-readable ASCII table output on stdout and exits 0; the table's column layout is not asserted to be stable across releases (no snapshot test pins its exact byte content beyond confirming it is non-empty and non-JSON).",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-009",
      "criterion": "In a workspace with three or more packages producing platformTargets entries, the keys of the platformTargets object in --format json output appear in strict lexicographic order by package name, and the keys of runtimeVersions likewise; within a single PlatformTargetGroup with two or more targets, the targets[] array is ordered by ascending triple string.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-010",
      "criterion": "Running `callisto matrix --format json` against a workspace containing a pyproject.toml with malformed TOML syntax (e.g. an unterminated string) exits with code 1 and prints an error identifying the unreadable/malformed manifest path; no MatrixReport JSON is printed to stdout.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-011",
      "criterion": "Running `callisto matrix --format json` against a workspace where a package.json's napi.targets array contains a triple not recognised by callisto_graph::napi::triple_to_role (e.g. \"sparc64-unknown-linux-gnu\") exits 0, emits a warning-level diagnostic identifying the unrecognised triple and the offending package, and excludes that triple from targets[] while still including any other recognised triples from the same or other packages in the report.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-012",
      "criterion": "For every one of the 18 triple strings that callisto_graph::napi::triple_to_role recognises (per its current match arms: aarch64-apple-darwin, x86_64-apple-darwin, x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, x86_64-unknown-linux-musl, aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, aarch64-unknown-linux-musl, x86_64-pc-windows-msvc, i686-pc-windows-msvc, aarch64-pc-windows-msvc, armv7-unknown-linux-gnueabihf, x86_64-unknown-freebsd, aarch64-linux-android, armv7-linux-androideabi, riscv64gc-unknown-linux-gnu, powerpc64le-unknown-linux-gnu, s390x-unknown-linux-gnu, wasm32-wasip1, wasm32-unknown-unknown), the matrix module's hostRunner/useCross table has exactly one entry, and every PlatformTarget produced for that triple has a non-empty hostRunner string and a boolean (never null/absent) useCross field.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-013",
      "criterion": "For every PlatformTarget produced by callisto matrix, artifactName equals the literal string \"native-\" concatenated with the triple field, e.g. triple \"aarch64-apple-darwin\" produces artifactName \"native-aarch64-apple-darwin\".",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-014",
      "criterion": "For every PlatformTarget whose platform is one of darwin, freebsd, android, or wasi/unknown-with-wasm32-arch, the JSON output's abi field is null (not the string \"null\", not omitted); for win32-platform targets the abi field is likewise null (never \"msvc\"); for linux-platform targets abi is a non-null string matching the abi derived from triple_to_role's ManifestRole::Platform for that triple.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-015",
      "criterion": "The compiled MatrixReport, PlatformTargetGroup, PlatformTarget, and RuntimeVersionEntry Rust types contain no field named `rid` and no field named `targetFrameworks`/`target_frameworks`; PlatformTargetKind has exactly two variants (napi, maturin) and RuntimeEcosystem has exactly two variants (npm, python) -- verified by attempting to deserialize {\"kind\":\"dotnet-aot\", ...} and {\"ecosystem\":\"dotnet\", ...} fixtures and asserting deserialization fails.",
      "is_error_case": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-016",
      "criterion": "After this change, .github/actions/callisto-action/action.yml no longer contains the literal fallback string '{\"platformTargets\":{}}' as the nativeMatrix source; it instead invokes `callisto matrix --format json | jq '[.platformTargets[].targets[]] | unique_by(.artifactName)'` (or an equivalent shell pipeline producing the same jq expression) to populate the nativeMatrix output.",
      "is_error_case": false
    }
  ],
  "linked_requirement": "REQ-007",
  "reasoning": "Key discovery during drafting: the design doc's section 3.1 triple table (.claude/specs/callisto-matrix.md) is NOT byte-identical to the actual triple_to_role match arms in crates/callisto-graph/src/napi.rs today. The doc lists wasm32-wasi and armv7-unknown-linux-musleabihf; the code recognises wasm32-wasip1 and wasm32-unknown-unknown instead, and has no musleabihf arm variant. Since REQ-007 explicitly mandates reusing triple_to_role and NOT duplicating the table, I anchored the spec's authoritative triple list on the actual code (verified by reading napi.rs directly) rather than the stale doc prose, and called this out explicitly in scope and AC-012 so the implementer builds the hostRunner/useCross/artifactName table against the real 18 triples, not the doc's list. Also discovered: triple_to_role's ManifestRole::Platform only carries platform/arch/abi -- it has no concept of hostRunner/useCross/artifactName, so that mapping is unavoidably NEW code in matrix.rs, keyed by triple, not an extension of napi.rs (consistent with the non-goal 'no modification to napi.rs'). Also discovered: callisto-manifests has no existing reader for [tool.maturin].targets or engines.node — python.rs only parses requires-python for a different purpose (Poetry 2.x project table) — so both are new manifest-reading code, called out in scope. Placed MatrixReport/PlatformTargetGroup/PlatformTarget/RuntimeVersionEntry in callisto-model (following the StatusReport precedent) but noted graph-layer placement is an acceptable alternative since this is an implementation/module-boundary decision, not a contract decision — the JSON shape and field names are what's load-bearing for AC purposes, not the crate they live in. Kept the composite-action (section 7 of design doc) optional per REQ-007's explicit 'nice-to-have if time allows' language, but made the action.yml wiring change (section 6.1 jq pipeline) a hard AC since REQ-007 lists it as a done_when item, not a nice-to-have."
}

