      "suggested_fix": "Add a task before T11 that gives matrix() its own manifest-discovery pass independent of the registered-package set: walk the workspace for package.json/pyproject.toml files (reusing IgnoreWalkLocator's ignore rules or a plain ignore::WalkBuilder) and read every one found, so a malformed manifest is surfaced as GraphError::Manifest rather than skipped. Alternatively, amend the T19 fixtures so each malformed manifest sits in a directory that ALSO contains a valid, named manifest of the other format (e.g. bad-py/pyproject.toml malformed + bad-py/package.json with {\"name\":\"bad-py\"}), which makes the package registered and forces matrix to read and fail on the malformed file — and state that constraint explicitly in the spec, since it narrows AC-010/AC-010b to manifests belonging to an already-registered package."
